questions.answer:
Article 19(1) guarantees to all citizens six freedoms:
  (a) freedom of SPEECH AND EXPRESSION;
  (b) freedom to ASSEMBLE PEACEABLY and without arms;
  (c) freedom to form ASSOCIATIONS, unions or co-operative societies;
  (d) freedom to MOVE FREELY throughout the territory of India;
  (e) freedom to RESIDE AND SETTLE in any part of the territory of India;
  (g) freedom to PRACTISE ANY PROFESSION, or carry on any occupation, trade or business.
[Sub-clause (f) — right to property — was removed in 1978 by the 44th Amendment.] These freedoms come with REASONABLE RESTRICTIONS in the interests of sovereignty, public order, decency etc.
